import PSTSEPPA.ABO.ForwardInductionTheorem45
import PSTSEPPA.ABO.ForwardInductionSourceReadySignedLocalStage

/-!
# ABO Theorem 4.5: k-retractable ambient Γ, globally retractable local H[C]

The certified full forward induction has so far been stated for
a FINITE globally generated/retractable labelled group. The
published theorem, however, needs only retractability of the
LOCAL group H[C] generated by the parent alphabet C, which
need not hold for the entire source ambient Γ.

If Γ is merely k-retractable and |C|≤k, the independently
verified subgroup theorem proves that the TRUE generated
H[C], with all outside generators made trivial, is
GLOBALLY retractable and generated. Moreover, original
signed Cayley skeleton admissibility automatically yields
admissibility of the ACTUAL root-normalized H[C] old stage.

We now APPLY full rank induction inside this generated
local group to conclude its EXACT signed Definition-3.22
whole-component cluster property, asking only the
published bridge-free lower C-stage hypotheses within
the local group. There is no assumption that Γ itself
is globally retractable.

The earlier certified source/local signed EGraph isomorphism
also identifies all true original/new directed signed
edge classes and every realized word path. To deduce the
cluster property for the ORIGINAL ambient Γ quotient,
one still must transport old component-tagged supporting
minima, off-skeleton status, and signed cluster shape;
those source-local reflection gates are being formalized
separately. This theorem does not silently supply them.

No new axiom/sorry, fake old edge or untagged coordinate
identification.
-/

namespace PSTSEPPA
namespace ABO

variable {ι Γ : Type*}
variable [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Group Γ] [Finite Γ]
variable {gen : ι → Γ} {A : Finset ι}

namespace CayleySubgraphSpec

variable (K : CayleySubgraphSpec gen A)

/-- Source rank-local H[C] forward cluster property:

Assume only original K admissibility, rank-k
retractability of Γ, C⊆A with |C|≤k, and the actual
bridge-free proper rooted stages of the resulting
normalized signed H[C]-skeleton.

Then the full attached proper-coset EGraph over
H[C] has the EXACT whole signed Definition3.22
cluster property. The ambient Γ need NOT be
globally retractable or globally generated. -/
theorem sourceKLocal_forwardExactSignedClusterProperty
    (hadm : K.AdmissibleForCosetExtension)
    (k : ℕ) (hk : KRetractable gen k)
    (C : Finset ι) (hCA : C ⊆ A) (hCk : C.card ≤ k)
    (root : K.Vertex)
    (hBridge :
      (K.intrinsicComponentLocalSlice C root).HasAllLowerRootedBridgeFree
        (K.sourceInductionLocalAdmissibility hadm C hCA root)
        (isGenerated_trivialCompletionGenerator gen C)
        (retractable_trivialCompletionGenerator_of_kRetractable
          gen k hk C hCk)) :
    (K.intrinsicComponentLocalSlice C root).HasExactSignedWholeComponentClusterProperty
      (K.sourceInductionLocalAdmissibility hadm C hCA root)
      (isGenerated_trivialCompletionGenerator gen C)
      (retractable_trivialCompletionGenerator_of_kRetractable
        gen k hk C hCk) :=
  (K.intrinsicComponentLocalSlice C root).exactSignedClusterProperty_of_allLowerRootedBridgeFree
    (K.sourceInductionLocalAdmissibility hadm C hCA root)
    (isGenerated_trivialCompletionGenerator gen C)
    (retractable_trivialCompletionGenerator_of_kRetractable
      gen k hk C hCk)
    hBridge

end CayleySubgraphSpec
end ABO
end PSTSEPPA
